================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

This app builds on the open-source work of e04. The following components are
included in, or ported into, this project and are used under the MIT License
reproduced at the end of this section.

1. DeepCW - web-deep-cw-decoder
   https://github.com/e04/web-deep-cw-decoder  (online: https://deepcw.cc/)
   Copyright (c) 2026 e04 - MIT License
   Used for: the "CW AI" decoder. The neural decoding models in
   app/src/main/assets (model_en_2026-10.onnx and model_en_narrow_2026-10.onnx,
   both from the 2026-10-27 MIT release, renamed) and the Kotlin port of the
   audio / spectrogram / CTC / streaming-decode / pileup pipeline under
   app/src/main/java/com/example/yaesucatcontroladv/deepcw/.

2. DeepRTTY
   https://github.com/e04/DeepRTTY
   Copyright (c) 2026 e04 - MIT License
   Used for: the overlapping-window streaming method of the CW AI decoder
   (StreamingMethod.OVERLAP, deepcw/data/OverlapMerger.kt), adapted from the
   DeepRTTY streaming receiver.

3. HamNoise
   https://github.com/e04/HamNoise  (online: https://e04.github.io/HamNoise/)
   Copyright (c) 2026 e04 - MIT License
   Used for: the neural noise reduction (DENOISE) for CW and voice - the C
   sources and model weights in app/src/main/cpp/hamnoise/ (the JNI bridges
   jni_bridge.c / jni_bridge_voice.c are part of this app).

